          deckDescription: 'A 36-card deck is used: six through ten, Jack, Queen, King, and Ace in each of four suits. There are no jokers; the deck is stripped of twos, threes, fours, and fives. All thirty-six cards are dealt and used in play.',
          suitDescription: 'The four suits may be Swiss (Roses, Bells, Acorns, Shields) or French (Hearts, Diamonds, Clubs, Spades). One suit is chosen as trump each deal; trump determines the order of strength for scoring.',
          rankDescription: 'Ranks are 6 (low) up to Ace (high), with Jack and 9 having special high values when they are in the trump suit. Non-trump cards follow Ace high down to 6; trump ranking differs for scoring.',
